# D50 (2026-08-28): `unsafe` is REMOVED from the language — the reserved
# keyword and all support. The function QUALIFIER spelling `unsafe <ret> f(...)`
# is gone; it is the removal's only accept -> reject flip.
#
# RED-verified: at f3feea79 this program compiled clean (`gg check` -> rc 0,
# "OK: no semantic errors"), because the qualifier parsed and was merely
# recorded on `FunctionQualifiers.is_unsafe`. So `check_gg_fails` FAILED
# pre-removal and passes after it.
#
# ⚠ NOT a claim that `unsafe` is rejected everywhere: `unsafe:` as a STATEMENT
# stays legal and now parses as an ordinary NAMED SCOPE — pinned by
# `unsafe_is_now_a_named_scope.gg`. Only the qualifier form is a parse error.
#
# Expected: parse error.
unsafe void danger(int x):
    print(x)

void main():
    danger(1)
